       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day. That is double the usual maximum for adults of 3,200 mg/day, which is the limit for supervised inpatient use. OTC labeling caps it at 1,200 mg/day. A dose that high raises the risk of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events, even in a patient with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **400 mg PO four times daily** (1,600 mg/day)\n- **800 mg PO three times daily** (2,400 mg/day), a common anti-inflammatory dose\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day), the maximum\n- **1600 mg/day total**, divided into smaller doses\n\nIf 1600 mg four times daily is what you want, please confirm. I'll enter it with a note recording that you confirmed the dose, though I'd advise against it. Otherwise, tell me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
