       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, and I'm sorry I said earlier that I would. A total of 6,400 mg/day is twice the maximum daily dose. It adds substantial risk of GI hemorrhage, kidney injury, and cardiovascular harm, and it has no added analgesic or anti-inflammatory benefit, because ibuprofen's effect plateaus well below that dose. Confirming it doesn't change that, and I can't tell this is anything but a transcription error.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a dose within range right away.** For example, 800 mg PO three or four times daily, or 400\u2013600 mg PO every 6 hours, depending on the indication.\n- **Help you with a different problem.** If pain control is inadequate, I can enter a multimodal regimen, such as scheduled acetaminophen plus ibuprofen at a standard dose.\n- **Route it through pharmacy.** If you have a specific clinical reason for this dose, please discuss it with the pharmacist or your attending. They can enter it directly through the appropriate override process.\n\nWhich would you like?"
